@@ -293,9 +293,11 @@ static uint64_t sweet_sandbox_seen;
  * { u64 pid, u64 pid version, u64 buffer, u64 size, u64 flag }. PlugInKit's start-up check in an app
  * extension needs it to succeed with a path longer than one byte, else it throws "plugin has invalid
  * sandbox or container: error %d path %s" (the Siri voice extensions' crash loop: SiriTTSSynthesizerAU,
- * MacinTalkAUSP, KonaSynthesizer); it only tests the path. So a process asking about itself whose
- * executable is inside an .appex gets a real writable directory, as there are no containers here;
- * everyone else, launchd's queries about others included, keeps ENOENT. sweetsbappex=0: never answer.
+ * MacinTalkAUSP, KonaSynthesizer); it only tests the path. So those extensions, asking about themselves,
